    {
      "text": "Make … friends of the mammon of unrighteousness, Luke 16:9 (D&C 82:22). ye have not been faithful in the unrighteous mammon, Luke 16:11. no unrighteousness is in him, John 7:18. do not obey the truth, but obey unrighteousness, Rom. 2:8. if our unrighteousness commend the righteousness of God, Rom. 3:5. Neither yield ye your members as instruments of unrighteousness, Rom. 6:13. Is there unrighteousness with God, Rom. 9:14. unrighteous shall not inherit the kingdom of God, 1 Cor. 6:9. what fellowship hath righteousness with unrighteousness, 2 Cor. 6:14. damned who … had pleasure in unrighteousness, 2 Thes. 2:12. God is not unrighteous to forget your work and labour, Heb. 6:10. I will be merciful to their unrighteousness, Heb. 8:12. shall receive the reward of unrighteousness, 2 Pet. 2:13. he is faithful … to cleanse us from all unrighteousness, 1 Jn. 1:9. All unrighteousness is sin, 1 Jn. 5:17.",
